Attribution Notes

This skill integrates data, knowledge, and tooling from multiple upstream
sources. The MIT license above covers original code & documentation written
for this project. Bundled data files retain their original sources' license
status as noted below.

1. breezyreeds/kangxi-strokecount (MIT) — BUNDLED
   File: assets/kangxi-strokecount.csv
   Author: Kawai Lo
   Repository: https://github.com/breezyreeds/kangxi-strokecount
   License: MIT (LICENSE preserved in CSV preamble)
   Contribution: Authoritative Kangxi stroke counts for 63,696 CJK characters
                 from Unicode 11.0. The data spine of this skill.

2. johnwu1114/chinese-name (NO UPSTREAM LICENSE) — BUNDLED WITH CAVEAT
   Files: assets/ChineseCharacters.json, assets/EightyOne.json,
          assets/Sancai.json, assets/zodiac/*.json (×12)
   Author: johnwu1114
   Repository: https://github.com/johnwu1114/chinese-name
   License: No LICENSE file declared upstream as of 2026-05-07.
            Author's stated intent: "免費的取名程式" (free naming program),
            suggesting permissive intent but not legally binding.

   The author's data is bundled here for educational and personal use.
   Anyone redistributing, forking, or using this skill commercially MUST:
     (a) Contact the original author (johnwu1114) for explicit permission, OR
     (b) Replace these files with self-curated equivalents, OR
     (c) Strip these files and use a reduced feature set.

   See README.md "License Caveat" section for details.

3. zh.wikiversity 生肖姓名學 (CC BY-SA 4.0) — DERIVED, NOT BUNDLED
   Source: https://zh.wikiversity.org/wiki/生肖姓名學
   License: CC BY-SA 4.0
   Contribution: scripts/zodiac_explain.py condenses ~186 radical-level rules
                 from this page into a Python data structure. The folk-knowledge
                 rules themselves (民俗) are public-domain; only Wiki's specific
                 wording is CC BY-SA. Rules in the script are paraphrased.
                 Source attribution preserved in zodiac_explain.py docstring.

4. 熊崎健翁《姓名 の 神秘》系統 — FOLK / PUBLIC DOMAIN
   Used in: scripts/lucky_81.py (81 靈動數),
            scripts/sancai_table.py (125 三才).
   These traditional naming-school tables originate from Kumagi Kenou's
   1929 Japanese book and have been in the public domain in Taiwan for
   decades. Specific吉凶 grade choices follow common 台灣命名師 conventions
   where schools disagree.

5. Anthropic skill-creator template — STRUCTURE INSPIRATION
   The skill scaffold (SKILL.md, scripts/, references/, assets/ layout) follows
   the Anthropic Claude Code skill convention.

6. Inspired but NOT bundled, NOT derived:
   - babyname/fate (https://github.com/babyname/fate) — initial reference for
     six-school 姓名學 architecture (this skill uses none of its code).
   - JakLiao/GoodGoodName, James88/qiming — reference projects only.
   - tony801015/chinese-lunar, cantian-ai/bazi-mcp — recommended companions
     for 八字 calculation, mentioned in SKILL.md but not bundled.
